   "Northwind-negotiator": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "competing",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 sets a 5% per-model cap but no sales stop: exceeding it triggers reporting, a corrective-action plan and retesting, and any sales restriction is discretionary, so the cap is largely non-binding for market access. S5 makes an 8-per-100,000 recall mandatory with no transition period, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) but does not ban sales. S3 gives a 6-year retrofit window, favouring Northwind, whose installed base is only 38% shut-off capable. S1's 24-hour rule applies to both companies, which each have unreported incidents."
 },
